From 97514d0127e4ac38c890267e630da2a0d38161ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CipherScope <dev@cipherscope.io>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 23:34:23 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 60/65] test: add script tests for P2MR leaf version 0xe0

test/util/generate_p2mr_tripwire_script_tests.py writes 83 rows of
script_tests.json, with real, deterministic Schnorr, ECDSA and ML-DSA-44
signatures, in a block just above the OP_CHECKMLDSA44 ones so that each
generator rewrites only its own. Under each combination of
P2MR_TRIPWIRE and P2MR_EC_DISABLED:

- without P2MR_TRIPWIRE a leaf of version 0xe0 at depth one is not
  executed, so an invalid signature passes, with P2MR_EC_DISABLED or
  without, and DISCOURAGE_UPGRADABLE_TAPROOT_VERSION makes it fail;
- with P2MR_TRIPWIRE alone it behaves as a leaf of version 0xc0: valid
  and invalid signatures, wrong sizes and hash types, OP_NOT, empty
  signatures, OP_CHECKSIGVERIFY, OP_CHECKSIGADD, empty and 33-byte keys,
  templates S1, S2 and S3, and the annex;
- with both, every check that reaches a 32-byte key with a non-empty
  signature fails as P2MR_EC_DISABLED, whatever the signature, and
  OP_NOT cannot turn that around; a 521-byte element still fails before
  the script runs, an exhausted validation weight budget still fails
  first, and empty signatures, empty and 33-byte keys, OP_CHECKMLDSA44
  and the ML-DSA-44 leaf of S3 are as before.

They also cover depth zero, the control byte 0xe0, OP_SUCCESSx in the
leaf, signatures made for the same leaf at the other leaf version, and
leaves of version 0xc0 and 0xfa, P2TR, legacy and P2WPKH spends under
P2MR_EC_DISABLED, which it does not change.

The functional test framework gets the leaf version 0xe0 helpers the
generator and the functional tests share, and mldsa44_sighash and
mldsa44_sign_input take the leaf version of the leaf they sign for.
